    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d242">

                <pb facs="0329" n="221" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg221"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr. Gresham</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-04-19"><hi rendition="#italic">April 19,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Egan reports that within an hour after the receipt, at 4 o’clock p.m. on
                    April 18, of Mr. Gresham’s telegram he communicated its substance to the Chilean
                    Government and requested that the refugees be protected when they should leave
                    the legation, as he was instructed to do; that one of the refugees, Fuentes, who
                    attempted to leave the legation, together with some visitors, at about 8 o’clock
                    in the evening, during Mr. Egan’s absence, was arrested at once on the street
                    and lodged in jail by the police, and that the other, Blanlot-Holley, who is
                    supposed to have left at about the same time, made his escape good through a
                    force of 300 detectives and police, at least, who were then surrounding the
                    block in which the legation is situated.</p>
            </div>
